.TH SHOAL-SECRET 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-secret \- manage encrypted Shoal secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-secret set
.I name
.br
.B shoal-secret list
.br
.B shoal-secret delete
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores exact secret bytes read from standard input, lists secret names, or deletes a named value.
Secret values are never printed by this command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI set " NAME"
Read a bounded value from standard input and atomically store it under NAME.
.TP
.B list
Print one secret name per line without decrypting values for output.
.TP
.BI delete " NAME"
Remove NAME from the encrypted store.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Only
.B list
produces normal output.
.B set
and
.B delete
are silent on success, and values are never echoed.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid UTF-8 names, oversized input, malformed invocations, unavailable key material,
and store or encryption failures are reported without printing secret bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
printf %s "$API_TOKEN" | shoal-secret set api-token
shoal-secret list
shoal-secret delete api-token
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 for store operation failures, and 2 for invalid invocation or store initialization.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1)
